looking-glass changelog. Most recent changes are at the top.

version 1.2 (2026-08-24)
feature:
  - agent: add `/http-check` endpoint — GET the target URL with redirects not followed (first response's status is reported as-is) and TLS verification enabled, returning status code, reason phrase, elapsed time, and the resolved IP; 10s total budget, same class as `/portcheck`
  - proxy: add `/api/http-check`, fanning out to all live nodes in parallel — same concurrency/liveness/capture pattern as `/api/ping-all`
  - validator: add `ValidateHTTPTarget` — requires an http/https-scheme URL, then runs the host through the existing `ValidateNotPrivate`
  - ui: new HTTP tab, positioned after Traceroute — table of Location/Result/Time/Code/IP per node, Copy Link and Permanent Link wired the same as every other tab
  - report: `http-check` added as a Permanent Link report kind, same wiring as the other six

version 1.1 (2026-08-10)
feature:
  - nodes: add background agent-liveness tracking — a goroutine polls every agent's `/health` endpoint every 12s (3s timeout, dedicated http.Client), marking a node dead after 2 consecutive failures and live again after 1 success; all nodes are optimistically treated as live until the first check round completes
  - handler: `/api/nodes` now returns `nodes.LiveNodes()` instead of the full static list — an unreachable agent is simply omitted, not flagged with a status field
  - proxy: `/api/ping-all` fans out only to live nodes — a dead node gets no entry in `results`, not a `status: "error"` row
  - proxy: `/api/proxy` and `/api/portcheck` check liveness immediately after the node lookup and fail fast with the existing "agent unreachable" error instead of waiting out the full agent-call timeout (130s / 10s) against a node already known to be dead

version 1.0 (2026-08-05)
feature:
  - report: add server-authoritative "Permanent Link" — freezes the actual result a check produced and serves it back from a stored copy for 24 hours, via new `POST /api/report/promote` and `GET /api/report` endpoints
  - handler: every check response (ping, ping-all, traceroute, portcheck, dns, ssl, bgp) now carries a `request_id` — a JSON field for request/response endpoints, an initial named SSE event (sent before any hop/result data) for the streaming ones — used to promote that specific result to a permanent report
  - bgp: `/api/bgp` response now also includes the normalized lookup `type` (`ip`, `prefix`, or `asn`)
  - main: new `REPORTS_DIR` environment variable (default `/var/lib/looking-glass/reports`) for where promoted reports are stored, following the existing `GEOIP_PATH` convention
security:
  - report: `/api/report/promote` is gated by its own 10-per-hour-per-IP limiter, independent of the general token bucket and the subprocess semaphores — a disk write is a different resource than a probe execution and needed its own dimension
  - report: both the ephemeral request ID and the promoted report ID are crypto/rand, 160-bit, fixed-length/charset, and validated before ever being used to build a filesystem path — the report ID becomes part of a public, unauthenticated URL
  - report: the persisted report store rejects new promotions outright once 2000 reports are active rather than evicting the oldest, since an existing report may be a link someone is actively sharing right now

version 0.9 (2026-08-01)
fixes:
  - handler: fix /api/ssl to parse host:port and ip:port directly from `target` (default port 443) instead of a separate `port` query param — the documented syntax was rejected by validator.ValidateTarget's hostname regex before ever reaching SSLCheck's splitting logic, making that logic dead code since day one; a dedicated field for a rarely-used option added UX friction for no benefit
security:
  - handler: rework clientIP to take the second-from-last X-Forwarded-For entry (the real client IP as observed and appended by the CDN edge in front of this deployment, confirmed via packet capture), falling back to X-Real-IP then RemoteAddr, fixing "Your IP" display and the rate-limit key showing the CDN edge IP for every visitor
  - handler: trust X-Real-IP before X-Forwarded-For in clientIP to stop per-IP rate-limit and subprocess-semaphore bypass via spoofed X-Forwarded-For
  - proxy: return a fixed "agent unreachable" message with no error text in Proxy and PortCheck instead of returning raw dial errors that leaked internal agent IP:port
  - proxy: gate Proxy and PortCheck behind the same per-IP and global subprocess semaphores as Ping/Traceroute/Dig
  - proxy: fix Proxy target validation bypass — the sanitized target was checked, but the raw unsanitized query was what actually got forwarded to the agent
  - handler: add periodic cleanup for the per-IP subprocess semaphore map to stop unbounded growth
  - handler: add rate limiting and a 50-target cap to /api/ip-info
  - proxy: validate targets in Proxy, PortCheck, and PingAll through internal/validator instead of ad hoc blacklists
  - proxy: bound PingAll's per-request agent fan-out to 8 concurrent requests instead of unconditionally spawning one goroutine per node
  - nodes: fail fast at startup if AGENT_SECRET is unset instead of silently sending an empty secret
  - validator: reject targets that are or resolve to a loopback, private, link-local, or multicast address (including 169.254.169.254) across ping, traceroute, portcheck, ssl, proxy, and ping-all
  - handler: rate-limit /api/bgp with the same per-IP token bucket used by other probe endpoints
  - validator: return the resolved IP from ValidateNotPrivate and pin it for ping/traceroute/ssl's actual connection, closing a DNS-rebinding window between the validation lookup and the real one
  - handler: drop the ValidateNotPrivate check from Dig — it only queries public resolvers about the target name and never connects to the target address, so the check had no SSRF benefit and incorrectly blocked legitimate PTR lookups against internal IPs

version 0.8 (2026-06-12)
frontend:
  - Split monolithic index.html into separate css/style.css and js/app.js
  - Changed embedding from single file to full directory embed (`//go:embed web`)
  - Added http.FileServer for serving static assets from embedded FS
  - Improved output escaping across render functions to reduce XSS risk:
    - renderTraceLine, renderBGP, renderDNS
    - Dynamic updates in ping results table
    - Error message rendering in multiple endpoints
docs:
  - Minor updates to INSTALL.md regarding web UI changes

version 0.7 (2026-06-11)
security:
  - nodes: load `Secret` from `AGENT_SECRET` environment variable instead of hardcoded value

version 0.6 (2026-05-26)
geoip:
  - Support multiple CSV sources via `GEOIP_PATH` and `GEOIP_PATH2`
  - Field-level merge when loading multiple sources (later sources take precedence for non-empty fields)
  - `/api/ip-info` now falls back to BGP origin AS + name when GeoIP data is missing or incomplete

version 0.5 (2026-05-25)
dns:
  - Major overhaul of DNS lookup (/api/dig)
  - Parallel queries to multiple resolvers (default: public reliable servers)
  - Clean grouped output instead of raw dig (shows "found on X resolvers")
  - New structured rendering in UI (card-based like SSL/BGP)
  - Added support for debug=1 parameter

ui:
  - Added "Copy Link" button to all panels (Ping, Traceroute, DNS, Port, SSL, BGP)
  - Shareable links with auto-run support (?tab=...&t=...&run=1)
  - Improved loadFromURL() for deep linking

api:
  - /api/dig now returns summarized results instead of raw dig output

version 0.4 (2026-05-10)
    traceroute: enrich hop IPs with ASN and operator name via ipinfo trie
    traceroute: batch hop enrichment to fix out-of-order line rendering
    ui: add /api/ip-info endpoint for batch GeoIP lookup without BGP lookup
    ui: fix pre terminal overflow on long lines
    ui: strip http/https prefix from user input before sending to server
    nginx: remove /api/ location block and error_pages include
    nginx: set limit_req_status 429 to return JSON-compatible error
    docs: update INSTALL.md to reflect nginx config and add error_pages warning


version 0.3 (2026-05-08)
    geoip: add ipinfo Lite CSV loader with radix trie and ASN index
    bgp: enrich IP lookup with country, continent, and AS operator data
    bgp: render AS path as directed chain with operator names
    ssl: strip internal server addresses from error messages
    ui: fix node selector not populating on traceroute and port tab switch

version 0.2 (2026-05-03)
    port: add multi-node TCP port check with open/closed/filtered status
    port: strip http:// and https:// prefixes before resolution
    ping: replace single-node SSE stream with parallel multi-node probe
    ping: render results as table with loss% and RTT min/avg/max per node
    agent: add /ping-summary endpoint returning parsed ping statistics
    agent: add /portcheck endpoint with 5s TCP connect timeout
    nodes: add IranianNet probe node

version 0.1 (2026-04-29)
    initial release
    master/agent architecture with pre-shared secret authentication
    ping and traceroute via SSE with source node selection
    BGP route lookup from local MRT dump via radix trie
    DNS lookup via dig
    SSL certificate inspection
    token bucket rate limiting per IP
    per-IP subprocess semaphore
    fail2ban integration
